  "body": "Found while working #1559 (issue-worker-high, upstream main ce59ef446).\n\n## What happens\n\nThe rapid law convicts \"rapid move N travels below the clearance plane inside stock\" - a rapid **at** the clearance plane is never judged. So when the clearance plane itself is set inside the stock (a Fixed height, or Top-of-Model + an offset smaller than the stock allowance), the op's traverse runs through uncut stock and the program **posts with no warning**.\n\nReproduced headlessly (synthetic fixture of `crates/app/tests/top_stock.rs`):\n\n- Stock box 40 x 40 x 10 (top Z10), part a 10 x 10 x 5 cube at the origin.\n- 2D Contour on the part, `clearance_z = Fixed 8`, `retract_z = Fixed 8`, Top 5, Bottom 0, stepdown 2.5, Plunge entry.\n- Generated path: move 0 `Rapid (0,0,8) -> (10.35,-2.98,8)` - a lateral rapid 2 mm under the stock top, through the stock; the machine also arrives at Z8 over (0,0), inside the stock column.\n- `tp.warnings == []`, and `posting::post_setup_unwritten` returns `Ok`.\n\nNothing at command creation refuses a clearance below the stock top either (Contour validation only checks clearance >= Top, retract >= Top).\n\n## Why P1\n\nA rapid through uncut stock is a collision that passes (AGENTS.md P1: \"a gouge or collision that passes\"). The default heights reference the stock top, so a user has to set the plane low, but a Fixed or model-referenced clearance on a taller stock is ordinary input.\n\n## Done means\n\n- A rapid at (not only under) the clearance plane that passes through stock the program ahead has not removed is convicted (`RapidInStock` or a named clearance-in-stock warning) and holds the post - or a clearance/retract plane under the remaining stock top over the op's travel is refused by name at generation.\n- Pinned by a test for the repro above (Contour) and one other ladder kind; the #96/#1066/#1091 rapid-law pins unchanged.\n\nRelated: #1559 (entry over carried stock), #96, #104, #1095.\n",
